00:16:12,560 --> 00:16:15,360
just a couple more thoughts that I would append to

254
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:18,320
what I had to say in last week's podcast about patrols.

255
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:21,760
after talking about the foundational ideas

256
00:16:22,480 --> 00:16:24,520
that Baden Powell had,

257
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:28,000
I want to say that one of our challenges is taking those ideas

258
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:31,520
and having those ideas inspire our methods

259
00:16:31,920 --> 00:16:34,280
so that our methods remain relevant.

260
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:36,960
Now we can't use exactly the same methods

261
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:39,160
that were used a century ago.

262
00:16:39,560 --> 00:16:41,960
We can use the same ideas, though,

263
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,880
And there are a couple of things at least

264
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:46,680
that make a lot of BP's methods

265
00:16:47,320 --> 00:16:50,880
and Green Bar Bill's methods about patrols

266
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:54,080
kind of impractical for us today.

267
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:56,760
But the ideas are solid.

268
00:16:56,760 --> 00:17:00,120
So separating method from idea

269
00:17:00,560 --> 00:17:02,800
is really the point of what I want to say here.

270
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:06,520
If you look at the methods that BP applied to patrols

271
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:09,560
and then Bill Hillcourt or Green Bar Bill

272
00:17:09,840 --> 00:17:12,880
advised us about, those exact methods

273
00:17:13,360 --> 00:17:18,520
need to be modified to meet the kind of societal

274
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:22,160
and cultural changes that have happened over the past century.

275
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:25,600
One of the things is that scouts are entering scout troops-

276
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:29,320
at least here in the BSA- at a much younger age

277
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:32,760
and developmental horizon than they did all those decades ago.

278
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:36,760
Originally boys had to be 12 years old to join a scout troop,

279
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:41,120
and a 12 year old, you know, from 1910 to 1950-

280
00:17:41,240 --> 00:17:45,120
would have been probably significantly more mature

281
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:47,080
than a 12 year old today,

282
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:51,120
And that's not saying anything about 12 year olds today.

283
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:54,280
It's more of a comment on the societal

284
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:56,520
and cultural norms of the day.

285
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:59,680
We delay certain cultural and societal norms

286
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:02,960
for 12 year olds today that they were expected to meet

287
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:07,680
decades ago, because we've expanded the number of years

288
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:09,400
that they spend in schooling.

289
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:12,200
So the difference between where our boys come to us,

290
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:15,560
that kind of developmental horizon where they come to us now

291
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:19,920
at 10 and a half, is going to be a pretty big sea change

292
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:23,440
from a 12 year old in the first 50 years of scouting.

293
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:26,640
The other thing that I think is an interesting societal

294
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:29,800
and cultural change is the mobility of children. today

295
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:33,280
There's not too many places where they're walking to school

296
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:36,600
or have their own neighborhood gangs on the same basis

297
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:39,200
as they did in that first 50 years of scouting.

298
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:44,440
So patrol cohesion over time becomes a little problematic,

299
00:18:44,440 --> 00:18:47,720
especially as their alliances and interest shift.

300
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:52,840
Again, I'm not saying that this is a problem for us to fight,

301
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:55,960
but just simply something that we should adapt to.

302
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:58,720
Now I've never suggested that really mixing ages

303
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:02,160
in patrols is an important thing

304
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:04,720
or necessarily even a good idea.

305
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:09,240
It's not unimportant or a bad idea either.

306
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:11,760
It's going to be different with different scouts

307
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:15,280
because as soon as you get eight personalities

308
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:17,240
of people that age together.

309
00:19:17,400 --> 00:19:20,200
some aspects of it may be predictable,

310
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:24,360
but you can't set detailed way of handling

311
00:19:24,600 --> 00:19:26,920
all of the different variables that are going to happen

312
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:28,440
in a situation like that.

313
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:31,480
What I was aimed at trying to point out last week

314
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:34,280
was, I think the problem is is that we have

315
00:19:34,280 --> 00:19:36,920
a pretty pervasive understanding that we adults

316
00:19:37,320 --> 00:19:39,880
should be engineering who is in what patrol,

317
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:42,880
And I think that is because we don't have a very clear

318
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:45,520
understanding of why we have patrols in the first place.

319
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:47,480
And going back to what the founder said,

320
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:49,560
he said the whole thing with patrols,

321
00:19:49,560 --> 00:19:52,360
the whole way that patrols work,

322
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:54,400
and the reason that we have patrols

323
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:56,080
is not to save scouter's time

324
00:19:56,080 --> 00:20:00,040
or not to impose an efficient management system

325
00:20:00,440 --> 00:20:02,080
on a group of scouts,

326
00:20:02,080 --> 00:20:04,720
But because it is all of the interactions

327
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:07,440
within the patrol is they do what scouts do

328
00:20:07,920 --> 00:20:11,240
that are truly aimed at developing

329
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:14,320
the kind of character we want to develop in scouting.

330
